rsz: run last gasp only after a main phase that was still gaining

Policy candidate from the repair-knobs campaign (ideas/repair-knobs-nihl.md),
carried while it is measured; retires SKIP_LAST_GASP if it dominates.
Not upstreamed.

Last gasp re-runs the sweep with a looser acceptance rule. When the main
phase ran out of endpoints while still gaining, that second pass pays;
when the main phase stopped because nothing was moving, the second pass
moves nothing either (riscv32i grt: 26% of the call for 0 ps). The main
phase now records whether it ended by its own termination test, and last
gasp runs only when it did not.

Chesterton's Fence: last gasp exists because some designs gain there
(ibex cts loses 2.8 ps without it), and SKIP_LAST_GASP exists because
others do not. The handover state distinguishes the two cases without a
knob. The knob is left in place and still honoured.

diff --git a/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh b/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh
index b38ade6a98..b2af33e112 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh
+++ b/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh
@@ -66,6 +66,9 @@ struct RepairSetupContext
   // Legacy-derived setup phases share one preamble per repair_setup run.
   bool legacy_preamble_done{false};
   bool legacy_preamble_has_violations{true};
+  // The main phase ended because it stopped making progress (its own
+  // termination test), not because it ran out of endpoints.
+  bool main_phase_stalled{false};
 };
 
 }  // namespace rsz
diff --git a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc
index 454cc2758c..f1dc7fd98c 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc
+++ b/src/rsz/src/policy/SetupLastGaspPolicy.cc
@@ -42,6 +42,17 @@ void SetupLastGaspPolicy::iterate()
     markRunComplete(false);
     return;
   }
+  // Last gasp re-runs the sweep with a looser acceptance rule. When the
+  // main phase ran out of endpoints while still gaining, that second pass
+  // pays; when the main phase stopped because nothing was moving, the
+  // census shows the second pass moving nothing either, for a quarter of
+  // the call. So it runs only after a phase that was still gaining.
+  if (setup_context_.main_phase_stalled) {
+    logger_->report(
+        "LAST_GASP skipped: the main phase ended without progress");
+    markRunComplete(false);
+    return;
+  }
 
   committer_.capturePrePhaseSlack();
   int& num_viols = setup_context_.violation_count;
